---
import LaundryHero from '../components/LaundryHero.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Workflow from '../components/Workflow.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Laundry lockers for laundromats | OurPort" description="Explore an indoor laundry locker wall for wash-and-fold drop-off and pickup. Keep pricing, processing and customer care with your team.">
  <section class="container laundry-hero" aria-labelledby="laundry-title"><div class="laundry-hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">For laundromat operators</p><h1 id="laundry-title">Make the wall <br /> work another shift.</h1><p class="lead">Give wash-and-fold customers a place to drop off and pick up when the site is open—even when the service counter is not.</p><a class="button" href="/plan-a-site/?role=laundromat">Plan your laundry wall <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><LaundryHero /></section>
  <section class="section container"><div class="three-columns"><article><p class="eyebrow">Customer convenience</p><h3>A handoff beyond the counter.</h3><p>Separate customer drop-off and pickup from staffed processing hours, wherever site access permits.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Operator authority</p><h3>Your service stays yours.</h3><p>You set the service menu, accept and price orders, manage quality and care for your customers.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Practical capacity</p><h3>Room for the real load.</h3><p>Size the locker around full bags and finished orders. Plan capacity from volume, turnaround and pickup patterns.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="operator-map"><div class="container"><div class="operator-map-heading"><p class="eyebrow">What changes—and what stays with you</p><h2>A new handoff point, built around your operation.</h2></div><div class="operator-map-grid"><div class="map-label">Customer</div><div><strong>Leaves and retrieves the order</strong><p>Uses the agreed access method and follows pickup instructions.</p></div><div class="map-label">Your team</div><div><strong>Accepts, prices, processes and returns it</strong><p>Keeps authority over service, quality, exceptions and customer care.</p></div><div class="map-label">OurPort</div><div><strong>Coordinates the locker service point</strong><p>Plans the configuration, access events and selected system connections.</p></div><div class="map-label">Property</div><div><strong>Approves the place and site rules</strong><p>Confirms access, network, monitoring and physical constraints.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <Workflow />
  <section class="section container split-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fit your existing operation</p><h2>Start with the way <br /> you work today.</h2><p>Which dashboard does your team use? Who accepts each order? What happens when a customer needs help?</p><p>Those answers shape the handoff. We review software compatibility, permissions and order events with you before agreeing an integration.</p><a class="text-link" href="/plan-a-site/?role=laundromat">Tell us about your operation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="review-list"><h3>We’ll work through</h3><ul><li>Full bag and finished-order fit</li><li>Customer access and processing hours</li><li>Order software, payment and notifications</li><li>Power, network and optional monitoring</li><li>Staff responsibilities and pickup exceptions</li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="container readiness-table"><div><p class="eyebrow">The first site conversation</p><h2>Useful answers. No finished specification required.</h2></div><div class="readiness-grid"><div><span>Bring</span><strong>Your current process</strong><p>How orders enter, who prices them, when work is processed and how customers are notified.</p></div><div><span>Estimate</span><strong>Demand and turnover</strong><p>Typical bags per day, peak periods, turnaround and how long finished orders wait.</p></div><div><span>Identify</span><strong>The likely wall</strong><p>A photo and approximate width are enough to begin; field verification follows.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="container download-strip"><div><p class="eyebrow">For owners, builders & developers</p><h3>Take the working concept with you.</h3><p>A three-page brief covering the service flow and site planning.</p></div><a class="button button-outline" href="/downloads/ourport-owner-builder-brief.pdf" download>Download the brief <span class="file-type">PDF · 3 pages</span></a></section>
  <CallToAction role="laundromat" title="What could your wall do?" body="Tell us about your wash-and-fold service, current setup and location. We’ll start there." />

</SiteLayout>
